'''Milner-Lemat Boulevard''' was a boulevard located on the pill that housed the [[Den of the White Worms|den]] of the criminal [[White Worms]] gang&mdash;formerly Syllain District Water Processing Plant Cresh&mdash;in [[Coronet City]] on the [[planet]] [[Corellia]]. The boulevard was located close to the edge of the pill by [[Antonian Lagoon]] and was a popular site for street racing<ref name="CLNE" /> in [[13 BBY]].<ref name="Date">''[[Star Wars: Timelines]]'' dates the events depicted on the Corellia page of ''[[Star Wars: Complete Locations, New Edition]]'' to [[13 BBY]].</ref>

==Behind the scenes==
Milner-Lemat Boulevard first appeared in the [[2018]] [[Star Wars Anthology Series|Anthology Series]] film, ''[[Solo: A Star Wars Story]]''.<ref name="Solo">''[[Solo: A Star Wars Story]]''</ref> It was first identified in the [[2025]] reference book ''[[Star Wars: Complete Locations, New Edition]]'',<ref name="CLNE" /> the new material for which was written by [[Jason Fry]] and [[Emily Shkoukani]].<ref name="Bluesky">{{Bluesky|jasoncfry.bsky.social|post/3ljusdhg5mc26|[[Jason Fry]]|date=2025-03-08|quote=Just got a copy of the newly revised Star Wars: Complete Locations from DK, out Tuesday! I wrote the updates with the peerless @shkouks.bsky.social. You'll find 12 new artworks, an updated galaxy map, new and reworked planet profiles, and details and Easter eggs galore. And a glorious cover!|archiveurl=https://ghostarchive.org/archive/CJuwQ|archivefile=File:JasonFry-CompleteLocationsNewEdition-Bluesky.png}} {{C|@shkouks.bsky.social confirmed to be [[Emily Shkoukani]] by {{Bluesky|tarkinstopshelf.bsky.social|post/3kjlh6aw5ry2k|[[Tarkin's Top Shelf]]|date=2024-01-22|quote=New Episode! #296: Dawn of Rebellion with @shkouks.bsky.social and @infinata.bsky.social! Your hosts welcome Emily Shkoukani and Pablo Hidalgo to the show! They discuss the creative process behind the Visual Guide and get to know their guests with some fun #StarWars questions!📚|archiveurl=https://ghostarchive.org/archive/eePoa|archivefile=File:TarkinsTopShelf-Shkoukani-Bluesky.png}}}}</ref> Actor [[Wikipedia:Paul Le Mat|Paul Le Mat]] portrayed the street racing character [[w:c:americangraffiti:John Milner|John Milner]] in [[Wikipedia:American Graffiti|''American Graffiti'']],<ref name="AmericanGraffiti">[[Wikipedia:American Graffiti|''American Graffiti'']]</ref> a [[1973]] film written and directed by ''[[Star Wars]]'' director [[George Lucas]].<ref name="YbY">''[[Star Wars Year By Year: A Visual History, New Edition]]''</ref>

